@page "/ministry"
@using CACI_Life.Features.SiteMedia
@inject ISiteMediaService SiteMedia

<SeoHead Title="CACI - Ministry Organization"
         Description="Meet the CACI Ministry: Bishops, Elders, and Ministers. Understanding our Apostolic structure."
         CanonicalUrl="https://caci.life/ministry" />

<section class="section-padding ministry-hero">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header">
            <h1>Meet the CACI Ministry</h1>
            <div class="divider"></div>
            <p>Three tiers of appointed or ordained leadership serving the Body of Christ.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ministry-grid">
            <div class="ministry-card elder">
                <img src="@SiteMediaHelper.GetUrl(_media, SiteMediaKeys.MinistryEldersImage)" alt="@SiteMediaHelper.GetAlt(_media, SiteMediaKeys.MinistryEldersImage)" onerror="@SiteMediaHelper.GetImageOnError(SiteMediaKeys.MinistryEldersImage)">
                <h3>Elders</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="ministry-card bishop">
                <img src="@SiteMediaHelper.GetUrl(_media, SiteMediaKeys.MinistryBishopsImage)" alt="@SiteMediaHelper.GetAlt(_media, SiteMediaKeys.MinistryBishopsImage)" onerror="@SiteMediaHelper.GetImageOnError(SiteMediaKeys.MinistryBishopsImage)">
                <h3>Bishops</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="ministry-card minister">
                <img src="@SiteMediaHelper.GetUrl(_media, SiteMediaKeys.MinistryMinistersImage)" alt="@SiteMediaHelper.GetAlt(_media, SiteMediaKeys.MinistryMinistersImage)" onerror="@SiteMediaHelper.GetImageOnError(SiteMediaKeys.MinistryMinistersImage)">
                <h3>Ministers</h3>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-padding ministry-body">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>The CACI Is Structured According to these first century Offices...</h2>

        <p>Because the CACI ordains "Bishops", a common misconception is that these titles must have some connection
            to Rome. However, Apostle, Bishop, Elder, & Minister are all titles used by the Original Apostolic
            Church in the New Testament. They are therefore the property of the True Apostolic Church today.</p>

        <h3>Worldwide Overseers</h3>
        <p>The Apostolic Council</p>

        <h3>Area/Regional Overseers</h3>
        <p>A District Council of The Regional Bishop & Local Pastoral Eldership</p>
        <p>The Bishop serves as a Sr. Pastor over all Congregations within his region.</p>
        <p>The Elders serve as Congregational Site Pastors in every city, extending the sacramental ministry of the
            Bishops into each Congregation.</p>

        <h3>Local Ministries</h3>
        <p>CACI Ministers</p>
        <p>The Ministers are nonexecutive ministerial assistants who are appointed to diverse tasks within the
            Congregations.</p>

        <h3>The CACI Apostolic Council</h3>
        <p>Executive Board of Directors (3 to 12 Member Council)</p>
        <p>This Council is made up of Bishops selected to serve in the office of the Apostles overseeing the
            direction of the CACI work worldwide.</p>

        <h4>Growing The Number to Twelve</h4>
        <blockquote>Luke 6:13 He called unto him his disciples: and of them he chose twelve, whom also he named
            Apostles</blockquote>

        <h4>Maintaining The Number at Twelve</h4>
        <blockquote>Acts 1:24-26 They prayed, and said, "You, Lord, who knows the hearts of all men, shew which of
            these you have chosen, that he may take part of this Ministry and Apostleship, from which Judas by
            transgression fell", And they gave forth their lots; and the lot fell upon Matthias; and he was numbered
            with the eleven Apostles.</blockquote>

        <h4>Unique Ministry of The Twelve</h4>
        <blockquote>Acts 6:2 So the Twelve called a meeting of all the believers. They said, “We Apostles should
            spend our time teaching the word of God..."</blockquote>

        <p>One member of this council is selected to serve as "first among equals" (Presiding Bishop), aided by two
            other members to assist (as pillars) in order to handle correspondence, prepare the agenda, conduct
            orderly meetings, and respond to special needs between Convocations.</p>
        <blockquote>Galatians 2:9 James, Cephas, and John, who seemed to be pillars</blockquote>

        <p>The CACI can only consider for this office those who, over a substantial length of time, have
            demonstrated their unwavering unity and support of...</p>

        <h3>THE MESSAGE OF THE CACI</h3>
        <p>Preaching The 4 Keys of The Kingdom</p>
        <ol>
            <li>The "Coming" Kingdom - Restored in the Earth forever</li>
            <li>The Culture of The Kingdom - The Kingdom celebrations & holy lifestyle spiritually revealed in
                Torah.</li>
            <li>The Law of The Kingdom - Originally written by the finger of God and kept in the ark.</li>
            <li>The Gospel of The Kingdom - A 2nd Exodus of the Blood-Water-Spirit</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>THE MISSION OF THE CACI</h3>
        <p>Restoring The 4 Pillars of The Apostolic Church - Acts 2:42</p>
        <ol>
            <li>The Apostle's Doctrine - Torah as spiritually taught & applied in the New Covenant</li>
            <li>The Apostle's Fellowship - A living and unbroken structure of rightly ordained Ministers</li>
            <li>The Apostle's Breaking of Bread - Apostolic sacramental authority</li>
            <li>The Apostle's Prayer - The spiritual conduit through which the Holy Spirit presides in the Body of
                Believers</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>

@code {
    private IReadOnlyDictionary<string, SiteMediaItem> _media =
        new Dictionary<string, SiteMediaItem>(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        _media = await SiteMedia.GetAllAsync();
    }
}
